{
  "abstract": "A complete Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of Conjecture 61 of DeLaViña's \"Written on the Wall II\" (conjectures of Graffiti.pc): for every finite simple connected graph G on at least two vertices, the number f(G) of vertices of a largest induced forest satisfies f(G) ≥ residue(G) + ⌈diam(G)/3⌉, where residue(G) is the Havel–Hakimi residue of the degree sequence. The formal statement is the one recorded in google-deepmind/formal-conjectures (WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture61.lean, theorem `conjecture61`, tagged research open there on 26 November 2026), copied verbatim together with its definitions of the residue and of `largestInducedForestSize`. The proof marks ⌈diam/3⌉ disjoint edges on a diametral geodesic and proves a new lemma: if a vertex set U induces a perfect matching, there is an independent set S outside U with residue(G) ≤ |S| + ⌈|U \\ N(S)|/2⌉. The lemma is obtained by a maximum-degree deletion argument with the matching re-paired in deletion order; the classical fact that deleting a maximum-degree vertex does not decrease the residue is proved from the Havel–Hakimi recursion.",
  "authors": [
